          "message": "check --claims: close XC1 re-check 5 (URL host boundary, BOM)\n\n- W2: run and commit URL patterns matched github.com inside another host\n  name, so \"agithub.com/.../runs/<id>\" was SUPPORTED at exit 0. Both now\n  start at a host boundary; github.com and www.github.com still count, a\n  subdomain or a longer host name is unread and blocks the text.\n- readClaimsFile drops one leading byte-order mark. Windows PowerShell 5.1\n  writes one for Out-File and Set-Content -Encoding utf8, and it made line 1\n  non-ASCII, so such a file could never decide. Only that one is dropped.\n\nW1 (an exclusion-only \"Locally\" paragraph above a claim) is not changed:\nthe claim's verdict stays within its scope, the cited run, and the text\nstill exits 3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
